# module Meson vendored integration adapter

Detect a consumer root `meson.build`. This adapter applies only to a `meson` export whose
dependency has a locked vendor; Meson has no native Git dependency form owned by this adapter.

# decision A generated subproject include and one owned root line

Write sorted `subproject('<id>')` blocks to the wholly tool-owned `deps/git-a2a/meson.build`. The root
file gets exactly `subdir('deps/git-a2a') # git-a2a`; remove only that marked line and only when no managed
dependency remains. Wire regenerates the generated file after any foreign content and warns that
the content was discarded. Unwire repairs or removes the generated file and never treats foreign
content as an ownership conflict.

# invariant Meson vendor paths are real subproject directories

Meson rejects path traversal in a wrap `directory` key. A dependency therefore uses the explicit
vendor path `subprojects/<id>` and has no dependency/export subpath; the generated include calls
that real subproject by id. Reject any other path with the exact corrective `set --vendor-path`
command. This avoids symlinks and works on Windows.

# test Golden and real-toolchain lifecycle

Fixture tests cover Wire, byte-identical second Wire, Drift, path rejection, foreign-content
repair, Unwire restoring root bytes, and sorted blocks. `GITA2A_IT=1` runs setup and compile with
Meson and Ninja in the pinned integration image.
